{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfiwjbRSCcPUnaXmiqRXJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DdAH29x413iSgnyheZ4wN3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_4\nS=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/second_order_chance_motif_suspicion.py\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `second_order_chance_motif_suspicion`: people still judge a sequence random to the extent their own second-order model of a fair coin (a person-specific believed switch rate, and a shared shift in how likely a switch is right after a switch) explains it better than the regular generators (a switch-biased Markov coin, a biased coin, and a repeating short motif with slips, with each person's own suspicion of motifs), the evidence weighed per flip by a fitted power of length. The single change, taken from `person_side_habit_switch_belief`, is that each person also has their own habitual leaning towards the Left or the Right button, drawn from a population, which adds to the randomness evidence before the choice, so when the two sequences look about equally random a person's side habit decides — addressing the FDR-surviving critique that participants' proportions of Left choices vary more across people than the incumbent produces.\nEOF\necho second_order_motif_side_habit > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - \"$S\" \"$D/candidate.py\" << 'PY'\nimport sys\nsrc=open(sys.argv[1]).read()\nsrc=src.replace('\"\"\"Second-order chance coin in the person-specific motif-suspicion judgment.\\n',\n'\"\"\"Person-specific side habit added to the second-order chance coin motif-suspicion judgment.\\n\\nRefinement of `second_order_chance_motif_suspicion`: the single change is that each\\nperson has a habitual leaning to the Left or Right button (non-centred population\\nwith a shared mean, 400 slots), added to the decision variable outside the\\nlength-scaled randomness evidence, so it decides near-ties. Taken from\\n`person_side_habit_switch_belief`. Addresses the critique that per-person Left\\nchoice rates vary more than the incumbent produces.\\n\\nDescription of the incumbent follows.\\n',1)\nold='    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta))'\nnew='''    # Person-specific side habit (non-centred population, shared mean bias).\n    mu_side = pm.Normal(\"mu_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.5)\n    sigma_side = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_side\", sigma=0.3)\n    z_side = pm.Normal(\"z_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    side = mu_side + sigma_side * z_side\n\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta + side[pid]))'''\nassert old in src\nopen(sys.argv[2],'w').write(src.replace(old,new))\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1505,"cache_read_input_tokens":77494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1505,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f54187ac-2111-4978-a75a-2d8868fdaf71","uuid":"e2bf19db-c7ff-44c6-a00b-aa7b3a685877","timestamp":"2026-10-05T10:37:43.814Z","request_id":"req_011Cfiwjb1PSmLtE1mSouWaV"}
