{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfiyTu4d4zDT5GTrhVPJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the admission check (`OK`). Its smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was -2096.8, against the incumbent's -2105.0. That is a rough signal only: the smoke fit was one short chain, not a production fit.\n\n**Model:** `second_order_motif_side_habit`, a refinement of the incumbent `second_order_chance_motif_suspicion`.\n\n- **What stays the same:** all of the incumbent's mechanism. People compare a second-order \"fair coin\" against the regular generators (a Markov coin, a biased coin, and a repeating motif). Each person has their own believed switch rate, suspicion of motifs and decisiveness, and the evidence is weighed per flip by a power of length.\n- **The one change:** each person also has a habit of leaning towards the Left or Right button, taken from `person_side_habit_switch_belief`. It is drawn from a population with a shared mean (non-centred, 400 slots) and added to the decision outside the length-scaled evidence, so it mostly decides near-ties.\n- **Why:** the critique found, with a result that survives the false-discovery-rate correction (q = 0.04), that people's rates of choosing Left vary more than the incumbent produces.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Reliability:** the check flagged the PSIS-LOO estimate as unreliable, with 8.1% of trials having Pareto k > 0.5. That likely comes from the many per-person parameters, but I didn't compare it with the incumbent's own diagnostics.\n- **Convergence:** not verified, because a single chain can't report R-hat. Admission's full fit decides that.\n- **Speed:** the 100+100 draw smoke fit took 330 s. The full fit has to finish within the 30-minute limit.\n- **Novelty:** not checked here. The risk is that the side habit averages out across participants on the novelty pool, leaving predictions close to the incumbent's.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":86177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":210,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":731,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f54187ac-2111-4978-a75a-2d8868fdaf71","uuid":"7f2fa5b0-53ee-419b-914c-36d792aa6bf3","timestamp":"2026-10-05T11:00:22.141Z","request_id":"req_011CfiyTtdL2rngZA3xT3Jv5"}
